# Strategy 6 — Pure HA Pattern Reversal After Streak
#
# Pure Heikin Ashi pattern strategy: enter on a color flip after a
# sustained N+ same-color streak (ha_bullish_reversal /
# ha_bearish_reversal), exit on the first OPPOSITE-direction strong
# candle (directional exhaustion).
#
# Design note — undirected vs directional exit:
# The originally-considered v1 used the zero-arg ha_strong() for both
# exits to demonstrate the undirected variant. In a LONG position
# that fires on EITHER bullish OR bearish strong candles, including
# bullish ones (which are in our favour) — a semantically debatable
# choice. The SPX2020 backtest with the zero-arg exit produced 932
# trades at streak_length=3 and 309 even at streak_length=8: the
# undirected exit churns positions immediately on the first strong
# candle either way, drowning the reversal-entry signal.
#
# Switched to the directional variants in the long/short exit
# Scenarios: ha_strong_bearish() for long exits, ha_strong_bullish()
# for short exits. This matches the strategy intent (exit on
# directional exhaustion against the position) and produces a
# readable number of trades. The zero-arg form is still exercised
# elsewhere in the catalog (none of the other demos use it; a
# follow-up "any-strong-candle alert" diagnostic Scenario would be
# the right home for it once §15 lifts the diagnostic-Scenario
# restriction).

Feature: Pure HA Pattern Reversal After Streak
  Primary timeframe: 1h
  Parameter streak_length default 3
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 1.5
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 4

  Scenario: Enter long on bullish reversal after bearish streak
    Given no open position
    When ha_bullish_reversal(streak_length)
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long on bearish strong candle
    Given a long position is open
    When ha_strong_bearish()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on bearish reversal after bullish streak
    Given no open position
    When ha_bearish_reversal(streak_length)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short on bullish strong candle
    Given a short position is open
    When ha_strong_bullish()
    Then short_exit
